{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvery operator-seeded SSM `SecureString` secret managed by `infra/terraform` persists its\nCLEARTEXT value in the remote terraform state (S3 `rebar-tfstate-896586841071`, key\n`rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate`, SSE-S3 not a CMK). The `value = \"CHANGEME\"` +\n`lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }` pattern stops terraform WRITING the secret from git, but\nterraform still READS the live value into `attributes.value` on every refresh/import, so the\nplaintext lands in state. This collapses the secret tier to the state-bucket ACL (`terraform state\npull` renders 23 secrets in cleartext to any state-bucket reader), and versioning retains the tail\nacross rotation. Root cause is proven; see the evidence comments below.\n\n## Decision (operator-approved — Option 1)\n\nMigrate every operator-seeded SSM `SecureString` SECRET from the `value = \"CHANGEME\"` +\n`ignore_changes = [value]` pattern to terraform WRITE-ONLY arguments `value_wo` + `value_wo_version`.\nWrite-only arguments are, by design, NEVER persisted to state (AWS provider docs: \"write-only values\nare never stored to state\"). Non-secret `String` config params (`jira-url`, `jira-user`,\n`jira-project`) and the terraform-GENERATED `SecureString` `opcert_origin_guard` (its value is\n`random_password.opcert_guard.result`, already in state via the random resource + the API-Gateway\nheader, so `value_wo` gives no net benefit) are OUT of scope and stay as-is.\n\n## Approach\n\nThree resources carry the seeded-secret antipattern and migrate to `value_wo` +\n`value_wo_version = 1` (dropping `value` and `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`):\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets` (for_each, 18 params) — `infra/terraform/ssm.tf:90`\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.opcert_ed25519_key` — `infra/terraform/opcert.tf:52`\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.cookie_signing_secret` — `infra/terraform/auth_sso.tf:39`\n\n`value_wo` requires `value_wo_version` (AWS provider ≥ 5.79) and write-only args require terraform\n≥ 1.11 (host: terraform 1.15.8, provider/lock 5.100.0). Raise the `versions.tf` floors, which today\nsit below those: `required_version` `>= 1.10` → `>= 1.11`; AWS provider `~> 5.0` → `~> 5.79`.\nRationale: write-only args are the provider-native mechanism purpose-built for keeping a secret out\nof state — no new dependency, no secrets-manager, no KMS CMK, minimal blast radius.\n\n### Steady-state no-clobber, and the one-time CUTOVER reset (explicit)\n\nIn STEADY STATE the write-only value is only (re)sent when `value_wo_version` changes, so an operator\nwho seeds a value out-of-band is never reverted by a later `apply`, and `user_data.sh`'s `CHANGEME`\nfail-fast still fires on an unseeded slot. The MIGRATION apply is different and is called out\nhonestly: because `value_wo_version` transitions from ABSENT to `1` (a change), the provider WILL\nsend `value_wo = \"CHANGEME\"` once and RESET each already-seeded parameter's live value to the\nplaceholder on that single apply. This is acceptable and intended here because the same exposure\nrequires ROTATING the exposed secrets anyway: the deferred operator ticket performs the migration\napply and the re-seed/rotation in ONE maintenance window (apply → every affected slot is now\n`CHANGEME` → operator seeds the NEW rotated value into each via `aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite`),\nwith `user_data.sh`'s `CHANGEME` fail-fast as the safety net against booting on a placeholder. The\nnew runbook documents this cutover sequence and a back-out note; the code change itself does not run\nany apply.\n\n### Unenumerated consumers of the old `ignore_changes` contract (updated in this change)\n\nTwo GATING consumers assert the opcert key still declares `ignore_changes = [value]` and must move to\nthe new write-only invariant in lockstep, or they regress to RED:\n- `infra/terraform/opcert-plan-assertions.sh` assertion (f) — rewrite to assert the key param\n  declares `value_wo` (+ `value_wo_version`) instead of `lifecycle.ignore_changes`.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` — `test_terraform_both_securestring_params_present`\n  (key-param `ignore_changes` assertion) and `test_assertion_script_present_executable_and_literal`\n  (asserts the script's `.lifecycle_meta_arguments.ignore_changes` literal) move to the `value_wo`\n  invariant; the `opcert_origin_guard` guard-param assertions are unchanged.\nTwo directly-related DOCS describe a migrated resource's old mechanism and are updated to the new one:\n`infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md` (cookie-signing-secret row) and `infra/runbooks/gerrit-auth-hardening.md`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/ssm.tf`, `infra/terraform/opcert.tf`, `infra/terraform/auth_sso.tf` — migrate the\n  three secret resources to `value_wo`/`value_wo_version`.\n- `infra/terraform/versions.tf` — raise the terraform + AWS-provider floors.\n- `infra/terraform/opcert-plan-assertions.sh` — assertion (f) → `value_wo` invariant.\n- `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` (NEW) — hermetic structural guard (no live AWS) that parses\n  `infra/terraform/*.tf` and, for every `aws_ssm_parameter` of `type = \"SecureString\"`, flags the\n  persisted-secret antipattern (a quoted string-literal `value` and/or `ignore_changes = [value]`),\n  requires `value_wo` be paired with `value_wo_version`, and allows the generated-value case\n  (`value` = an unquoted expression, no `ignore_changes`). Modeled on\n  `scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`.\n- `Makefile` — wire the new guard into `make lint` (next to `check_templatefile_escapes.py`, `Makefile:302`).\n- `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py` (NEW) — pins RED→GREEN + mutation teeth + committed-tree\n  clean + make-lint wiring, mirroring `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py`.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` — update the two consumers above to the `value_wo` invariant.\n- `docs/adr/0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md` (+ `docs/adr/.numbers/0105`, regenerated\n  `docs/adr/README.md`) — record the decision, extending ADR 0008, relating to ADR 0046.\n- `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` (NEW) — declare/seed/rotate via write-only args + the\n  operator REMEDIATION + CUTOVER sequence.\n- `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md`, `infra/runbooks/gerrit-auth-hardening.md` — refresh the stale\n  `ignore_changes` descriptions to the write-only mechanism, cross-linking the new runbook/ADR.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED first: the new guard/test fail against the CURRENT tree for the right reason (three\n  SecureString secrets persist a `value` literal + `ignore_changes = [value]`); proven before the fix.\n- GREEN after: guard + test pass once the three resources use `value_wo`/`value_wo_version`.\n- Mutation teeth: reverting any one param to `value = \"…\" + ignore_changes = [value]` returns the\n  guard to RED (asserted by `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py`).\n- `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` passes (static schema/argument validation; no\n  plan/apply against the real backend — the prod cutover is the deferred operator ticket).\n- The updated `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` passes against the migrated `opcert.tf` and\n  assertion script; `make lint` passes (ruff + the new guard + siblings).\n\nNo secret VALUE is printed, logged, or committed by the fix or its verification — the guard inspects\nHCL structure only, never values.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All three seeded-secret `SecureString` resources (`rebar_secrets`, `opcert_ed25519_key`,\n      `cookie_signing_secret`) use `value_wo` + `value_wo_version` and carry no `value`/`ignore_changes\n      = [value]`; verified by `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` exiting 0 and by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` is RED on the pre-fix tree and GREEN on the post-fix tree,\n      and a one-param mutation returns it to RED; verified by `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py`.\n- [ ] The guard is wired into `make lint`; verified by a wiring test and by `make lint` exit 0.\n- [ ] `versions.tf` floors are terraform `>= 1.11` and AWS provider `~> 5.79`; verified by reading the file.\n- [ ] `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` succeeds; verified by its exit 0.\n- [ ] `opcert-plan-assertions.sh` (f) and `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` assert the\n      `value_wo` invariant (not `ignore_changes`) and pass; verified by running the opcert test file.\n- [ ] ADR 0105 exists with marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0105`, the index is regenerated, and\n      `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` + `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` pass.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` covers declare/seed/rotate + the exposure-remediation\n      CUTOVER sequence and cross-links ADR 0105; verified by reading it.\n- [ ] A deferred OPERATOR `task` ticket for the prod remediation (apply → re-seed/rotate exposed\n      secrets in the same window → verify no SecureString value in `terraform state pull` → rotate\n      crown-jewels) exists and is linked `discovered_from` this ticket; verified by `show_ticket`.\n      [non-codebase] evidence: the new ticket id recorded in a comment.\n- [ ] No credential value is printed, logged, or committed by the fix or its verification."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788024158323830012,"uuid":"081aa4fd-fd7c-4306-90a7-c38602e34e67"}